/-!
# The n ≥ 44 pieces and strip atlas: parameters

The 55 pieces at `n ≥ 44` (0-based `p`): the sub-bands of the final configuration
(Profile30's 30 bands, 16 of them split).  Per piece: its edges
`pieceLo`, `pieceHi`, its parent band `pieceParent`; per band its first piece `pieceFirst` and its number of pieces
`pieceNsub`; the containing n ≥ 45 piece `pieceUp`; the O3 ladder row at `t = 0` used on the piece (`newEll`, `newA`:
the rate and potential coefficient, `0` = none; `rowOf`: its index in the O3 ladder rows, `26` = none); the five rates
`rates44` (the parent's, with `newEll` at `t = 0` on the rows); the caps `theta44`, `D44` (the configuration's
O2/O1 refits, else the parent band's); the O5 rank `kmin` and the floor `mmin = k/(2 q(pieceHi))` at
`n ≥ 44` (proved separately).  The strip of piece `p` is
`[q(pieceLo), q(pieceHi)] × [mmin44_p, N45.Data.mmin45_(pieceUp p)]` (up to the floor at `n ≥ 45` of the containing
piece) with the piece's caps and rates.  This file imports only Lean's core.
-/

